      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two issues here:\n1. Platforms other than skylake using npcx might not need to trigger a PMIC reset. This was just a workaround for the power topology specifically on skylake platforms derived from glados.\n\n2. On Fizz, since you removed CONFIG_CHIPSET_HAS_PLATFORM_PMIC_RESET, if the board runs into a panic/watchdog reset, then the x86 domain could end up in a weird state since the pmic reset won\u0027t be triggered there.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 740,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 743,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "3ca67ae9ef9483c482d9d8f51704734aa19b25dc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "27c08833_3fb4d166",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 743,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-02-08T04:25:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you are looking to save an extra reset, I think we can do something like this:\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_CHIPSET_HAS_PLATFORM_PMIC_RESET\n     gpio_set_level(GPIO_EC_PLATFORM_RST, 1);\n#else\n     system_watchdog_reset();\n#endif\n\nThat way we won\u0027t have to do an extra EC reset when EC is asked to do a reboot and it comes down this path.",
      "parentUuid": "a93a7781_e59f771e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 740,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 743,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "3ca67ae9ef9483c482d9d8f51704734aa19b25dc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
